the pods would help. The "kubectl describe pod" command can show events that might indicate why the pod isn\'t starting. But the user hasn\'t used that yet. Wait, the available commands include "kubectl describe", so maybe using that on the affected pods would give more detailed information.\n\nBut the user\'s last step was getting the list of pods, and the next step is to check the logs or describe the pods. Since the pods are in ContainerCreating, perhaps the issue is with the container image not being accessible, or the pod\'s configuration (like volumes, environment variables) being incorrect. \n\nSo, the best approach is to first check the logs of the pods. If the logs aren\'t available yet, maybe the describe command would show the events. Let me proceed with checking the logs first. Let\'s pick one of the MongoDB pods, like mongodb-geo, and get its logs. If that doesn\'t work, then use describe.\n</think>\n\ntool name: exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd  \nreasoning: The MongoDB pods (e.g., mongodb-geo, mongodb-profile) are in "ContainerCreating" state, indicating they are not yet ready. To diagnose the root cause, I need to inspect the logs of these pods to identify startup errors, missing dependencies, or configuration issues. Using "kubectl logs" on the specific pods will reveal any immediate container failures or errors during initialization.', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': Usage(completion_tokens=533, prompt_tokens=4137, total_tokens=4670, completion_tokens_details=None, prompt_tokens_details=None), 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfacd-9a75-7aa3-9ead-50ab8f74b393-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 4137, 'output_tokens': 533, 'total_tokens': 4670}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additi