ly configured, leading to the container not being able to start. So checking the PV status is the next step.\n</think>\n\ntool name: exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd  \nreasoning: The PVC `geo-pvc` is bound, but the container is still in "ContainerCreating" state. To confirm if the volume is properly attached and accessible, I need to check the status of the associated PersistentVolume (PV). If the PV is not available or has errors, it could prevent the container from starting. Running "kubectl get pv pvc-4e872310-af4b-42a8-ab9e-18fbd9d31652 -n hotel-reservation" will reveal the PV\'s status and any potential issues with the storage configuration.', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': Usage(completion_tokens=1609, prompt_tokens=5757, total_tokens=7366, completion_tokens_details=None, prompt_tokens_details=None), 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cface-2b61-74d3-8923-69eb50e5fe23-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 5757, 'output_tokens': 1609, 'total_tokens': 7366}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='65f5e1eb-93b4-4054-b1af-2d9d78b3ff2b')]]
