ke one tool call at a time. The previous step was getting services, and now they need to get deployments. So, the next tool call should be to run "kubectl get deployments -n hotel-reservation" to check the deployment statuses. That will show the number of replicas, available replicas, and any errors in the deployments. \n\nAlternatively, maybe they should check the pods directly. But deployments are a higher-level abstraction, so checking deployments first would give an overview. If deployments are healthy, then the pods under them should be okay. But if a deployment is not healthy, that could indicate issues like failed rollouts or scaling problems.\n\nSo, the correct next step is to use exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd with the command "kubectl get deployments -n hotel-reservation". That will provide the necessary information about the deployments. After that, if any deployments are problematic, they can then check the pods for more details. But for now, the immediate action is to get the deployments.\n</think>\n\n', additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl get deployments -n hotel-reservation"}', 'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-b078a2f689584eee', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 361, 'prompt_tokens': 3640, 'total_tokens': 4001, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfacd-5e18-7341-87be-aa7377a2b0b7-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd', 'args': {'command': 'kubectl get deployments -n hotel-reservation'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-b078a2f689584eee', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 3640, 'output_tokens': 361, 'total_tokens': 4001}), ToolMessage(content='NAME                 