 might be failing. \n\nAlternatively, maybe the container is waiting for a specific volume to be ready. But since the PVC is bound, that\'s probably not the issue. Another possibility is that the container is waiting for a specific process to start, but the logs don\'t show that. \n\nSo, the best approach is to check the ConfigMaps for the init and failure scripts. Using kubectl to get the ConfigMap contents would help identify if there are any errors in the scripts. If the scripts are misconfigured or have errors, that could prevent the container from starting. \n\nTherefore, the next tool to use is exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd to get the ConfigMap details for mongo-geo-script and failure-admin-geo. That way, the user can inspect the scripts for any issues.\n</think>\n\ntool name: exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd  \nreasoning: The MongoDB container logs show successful recovery but the pod remains in "ContainerCreating" state. This suggests the issue may be with the init scripts or failure scripts mounted in the pod. To investigate, I need to inspect the contents of the ConfigMaps `mongo-geo-script` and `failure-admin-geo` to check for errors in initialization or failure handling scripts that might be preventing the container from starting. Running "kubectl get configmap mongo-geo-script -n hotel-reservation" and "kubectl get configmap failure-admin-geo -n hotel-reservation" will reveal the script contents.', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 546, 'prompt_tokens': 10546, 'total_tokens': 11092, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cface-bb63-7291-b74c-9511613ba637-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 10546, 'output_tokens': 546, 'total_tokens': 11092}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='647745b8-30ed-43af-a569-54901d1bd1d8'), AIMessage(content="<think>\nOkay, let's see. The user is trying to diagnose why the MongoDB pod for the geo service isn't starting. So far, they've checked the PVC and PV, which are bound correctly. The container logs show MongoDB starting up and recovering, but the pod is still in ContainerCreating state. The next step was to check the ConfigMaps for init scripts and failure handling.\n\nThe user's last tool call was to get the logs of all containers in the pod, which didn't show any errors. Now, they need to check the ConfigMaps. The reasoning is that the init scripts or failure scripts might have errors. So, the next step is to retrieve the ConfigMaps `mongo-geo-script` and `failure-admin-geo` to look at their contents. \n\nThe tool to use here is `exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd` with the command `kubectl get configmap mongo-geo-script -n hotel-reservation` and similarly for `failure-admin-geo`. But since the user can only make one tool call per step, they should start with one of them. Maybe start with `mongo-geo-script` first to check the init scripts. If that's okay, then check the other one. So the next tool call should be to get the ConfigMap for the init scripts.\n</think>\n\n", additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl get configmap mongo-geo-script -n hotel-reservation"}', 'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-bf7242d340fb41fe', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 302, 'prompt_tokens': 11583, 'total_tokens': 11885, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cface-d800-7682-910e-cdb8023d054c-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd', 'args': {'command': 'kubectl get configmap mongo-geo-script -n hotel-reservation'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-bf7242d340fb41fe', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 11583, 'output_tokens': 302, 'total_tokens': 11885}), ToolMessage(content='NAME               DATA   AGE\nmongo-geo-script   1      4m32s\n', id='37a8512a-14ad-4d80-8904-96db9e8b7518', tool_call_id='chatcmpl-tool-bf7242d340fb41fe'), HumanMessage(content='You are now in the thinking stage. Choose a tool from the available tools and justify your choice.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='81fae3d0-59ba-42c5-8e65-55f3c279cf42')]]
