th the command "kubectl get pv pvc-4e872310-af4b-42a8-ab9e-18fbd9d31652 -n hotel-reservation". But the user needs to make sure that the PV name is correct. \n\nAlternatively, maybe the PV is not properly configured, leading to the container not being able to start. So checking the PV status is the next step.\n</think>\n\ntool name: exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd  \nreasoning: The PVC `geo-pvc` is bound, but the container is still in "ContainerCreating" state. To confirm if the volume is properly attached and accessible, I need to check the status of the associated PersistentVolume (PV). If the PV is not available or has errors, it could prevent the container from starting. Running "kubectl get pv pvc-4e872310-af4b-42a8-ab9e-18fbd9d31652 -n hotel-reservation" will reveal the PV\'s status and any potential issues with the storage configuration.', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 1609, 'prompt_tokens': 5757, 'total_tokens': 7366, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cface-2b61-74d3-8923-69eb50e5fe23-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 5757, 'output_tokens': 1609, 'total_tokens': 7366}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='65f5e1eb-93b4-4054-b1af-2d9d78b3ff2b'), AIMessage(content='<think>\nOkay, let\'s see. The user is trying to diagnose why the MongoDB pod for the geo service isn\'t starting. So far, they\'ve checked the deployments, pods, and found that the pod is in ContainerCreating state. The logs aren\'t available yet, so they used kubectl describe pod to get more details. The describe output showed that the pod is pending, and the container is waiting to start. The PVC geo-pvc is bound, but the PV might be the issue.\n\nThe next step is to check the PersistentVolume (PV) associated with the PVC. The PVC\'s name is pvc-4e872310-af4b-42a8-ab9e-18fbd9d31652. By running kubectl get pv on that name, they can see if the PV is available and properly configured. If the PV is not available or has errors, that could be why the container isn\'t starting. So the tool call should be to get the PV details. That makes sense because if the PV is in an error state or not properly attached, the pod can\'t access the storage, leading to ContainerCreating state. Let\'s make sure the command is correct and the namespace is specified. The command would be "kubectl get pv pvc-4e872310-af4b-42a8-ab9e-18fbd9d31652 -n hotel-reservation".\n</think>\n\n', additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl get pv pvc-4e872310-af4b-42a8-ab9e-18fbd9d31652 -n hotel-reservation"}', 'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-8766de9585e0f478', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 375, 'prompt_tokens': 6801, 'total_tokens': 7176, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cface-77cc-7e51-b521-f7245258f6b7-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd', 'args': {'command': 'kubectl get pv pvc-4e872310-af4b-42a8-ab9e-18fbd9d31652 -n hotel-reservation'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-8766de9585e0f478', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 6801, 'output_tokens': 375, 'total_tokens': 7176}), ToolMessage(content='NAME                                       CAPACITY   ACCESS MODES   RECLAIM POLICY   STATUS   CLAIM                       STORAGECLASS       VOLUMEATTRIBUTESCLASS   REASON   AGE\npvc-4e872310-af4b-42a8-ab9e-18fbd9d31652   1Gi        RWO            Delete           Bound    hotel-reservation/geo-pvc   openebs-hostpath   <unset>                          3m45s\n', id='a3601a38-406b-408b-b193-d85eaba0ce33', tool_call_id='chatcmpl-tool-8766de9585e0f478'), HumanMessage(content='You are now in the thinking stage. Choose a tool from the available tools and justify your choice.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='c01d0272-2859-4f02-8f17-767efdba459c'), AIMessage(content='<think>\nOkay, let\'s see. The user is trying to figure out why the MongoDB pod for the geo service isn\'t starting. So far, they\'ve checked the deployments, pods, PVCs, and PVs. The pod is in ContainerCreating state, and the PVC is bound to a PV. The image is being pulled, but maybe there\'s an issue with the container itself.\n\nHmm, maybe the container isn\'t starting because of a problem with the MongoDB configuration or the init scripts. The pod\'s describe output mentioned volumes like init-script and failure-script. Maybe the init scripts are causing an issue. The user should check the logs of the init scripts or see if there are any errors in the pod\'s events related to those scripts.\n\nWait, the user tried to get logs for the main container but got an error because it\'s still in ContainerCreating. Maybe they need to check the logs of the init scripts or the failure script. Alternatively, maybe the container image is incorrect or there\'s a version mismatch. The image used is mongo:8.0.14-rc0, which is a release candidate. Maybe that\'s not a stable version, or there\'s a missing dependency.\n\nAnother angle: the pod\'s environment variables or configuration files might be missing. The describe output shows no environment variables, but maybe the ConfigMaps (init-script and failure-script) are not properly configured. The user could check the ConfigMaps to see if the scripts are correct or if there\'s an error in them.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the container is waiting for a specific resource that\'s not available. The PVC is bound, but maybe the volume isn\'t mounted correctly. The user could check the pod\'s events for any messages related to volume mounting failures. Also, checking the node\'s status to ensure it\'s healthy and has enough resources might help. But since the PVC and PV are bound, the issue is more likely within the container or the scripts.\n</think>\n\ntool name: exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd  \nreasoning: The PVC and PV are correctly bound, but the container is still in "ContainerCreating" state. This suggests the issue may lie with the container image, init scripts, or configuration. To investigate further, I need to check the logs of the init scripts or failure scripts mounted in the pod. Running "kubectl logs mongodb-geo-5d9cf968b9-ztqrl -n hotel-reservation --all-containers" will capture logs from all containers, including any errors during initialization or script execution.', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 514, 'prompt_tokens': 6125, 'total_tokens': 6639, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cface-8c79-7993-ad08-4a6d0044d523-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 6125, 'output_tokens': 514, 'total_tokens': 6639}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='55a15dd7-3f05-4a4a-bb68-c21cd60b585f'), AIMessage(content='<think>\nOkay, let\'s see. The user is trying to diagnose why the MongoDB pod for the geo service isn\'t starting. So far, they\'ve checked the deployments, pods, PVCs, and PVs, and everything seems to be bound and available. The pod is in a ContainerCreating state, and the image is being pulled, but there\'s no error yet.\n\nThe next step is to check the logs from all containers in the pod, including any init scripts or failure scripts that might be running. The user mentioned that the pod has volumes mounted from ConfigMaps named "mongo-geo-script" and "failure-admin-geo". These ConfigMaps might contain scripts that run during initialization or on failure, which could be causing the delay.\n\nBy using the command "kubectl logs mongodb-geo-5d9cf968b9-ztqrl -n hotel-reservation --all-containers", they can get logs from all containers, not just the main MongoDB container. This might reveal any errors from the init scripts or failure scripts that are being executed. If there\'s a problem with the scripts, like a missing file or a syntax error, it could prevent the MongoDB container from starting properly.\n\nAlternatively, if the scripts are trying to access the PVC or perform some setup tasks that are failing, the logs would show that. Since the PVC is bound and the PV is available, the issue is likely in the scripts or the container configuration. Checking these logs should provide more insight into why the container isn\'t transitioning to the Running state.\n</think>\n\n', additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl logs mongodb-geo-5d9cf968b9-ztqrl -n hotel-reservation --all-containers"}', 'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-93e42b38ae6f8743', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 365, 'prompt_tokens': 7149, 'total_tokens': 7514, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cface-a517-75d3-8421-2e876b7b23b4-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd', 'args': {'command': 'kubectl logs mongodb-geo-5d9cf968b9-ztqrl -n hotel-reservation --all-containers'}, 'id'