MongoDB pods. Wait, but the command can\'t be done in one go. So, the assistant should pick one pod first. Let\'s check the logs for mongodb-geo-5d9cf968b9-ztqrl. If that\'s not possible, maybe check the logs for the pod that\'s been in ContainerCreating the longest. Alternatively, maybe the user can check the logs for all pods in the namespace, but that\'s not efficient. \n\nAlternatively, maybe the user can check the logs for the pods that are in ContainerCreating. Since the assistant can only make one tool call, they should choose one pod to check. Let\'s go with mongodb-geo-5d9cf968b9-ztqrl. So the command would be "kubectl logs mongodb-geo-5d9cf968b9-ztqrl -n hotel-reservation". That should retrieve the logs for that specific pod, which might show any errors during container creation. If there\'s an error, that would indicate the root cause, like a missing volume, configuration issue, or dependency problem. If not, the assistant can proceed to check other pods.\n</think>\n\n', additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl logs mongodb-geo-5d9cf968b9-ztqrl -n hotel-reservation"}', 'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-9380f9a2b9440695', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 703, 'prompt_tokens': 5131, 'total_tokens': 5834, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfacd-b389-7792-91e1-c60b0fbad0f4-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_read_only_kubectl_cmd', 'args': {'command': 'kubectl logs mongodb-geo-5d9cf968b9-ztqrl -n hotel-reservation'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-9380f9a2b9440695', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 5131, 'output_tokens': 703, 'total_tokens': 5834}), ToolMessage(content='Command Rejected: