k again. \n\nAlternatively, they could check the pod events or logs again to see if there are any new errors. But since the user is in the mitigation phase, the next step is to confirm if the issue is resolved. If the pods are now in a Running state, then the problem is fixed. If not, they might need to look into other issues like resource limits or network problems. \n\nBut according to the previous steps, the script was fixed, so the pods should start correctly now. The user should wait a moment and then check the pod status again. If the pods are still not running, they might need to look into other factors, but based on the information, the main issue was the script's variable handling.\n</think>\n\n", additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl get pods -n hotel-reservation"}', 'name': 'exec_kubectl_cmd_safely'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-90683908a4e8a4e9', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 446, 'prompt_tokens': 17130, 'total_tokens': 17576, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfad2-b010-7ea2-83da-df1b871194bd-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_kubectl_cmd_safely', 'args': {'command': 'kubectl get pods -n hotel-reservation'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-90683908a4e8a4e9', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 17130, 'output_tokens': 446, 'total_tokens': 17576}), ToolMessage(content='NAME                                     READY   STATUS             RESTARTS        AGE\nconsul-5c696cc4dc-6s4xr                  1/1     Running            0               8m44s\nfrontend-6df8475df4-qcb4d                1/1     Running            0               8m44s\ngeo-57c7bd6d5c-s9b66                     1/1     Running            2 (7m51s ag