 is using \'s/\\\'$ADMIN_USER\\\'/\\"$ADMIN_USER\\"/g\', which replaces occurrences of \'$ADMIN_USER\' enclosed in single quotes. But in the script, the variables are inside single quotes, so the pattern should match. However, maybe there are other variables like $ADMIN_PWD, $ROOT_USER, and $ROOT_PWD that also need similar treatment. The user\'s sed command includes all four variables, so that\'s covered.\n\nAnother possibility is that the script is still using single quotes in some parts. Let me check the script again. The user\'s latest tool call is to apply the ConfigMap again, but the output from the previous get configmap shows that the script still has single quotes. So the sed command might not have executed correctly, or the changes weren\'t applied.\n\nWait, the user might have made a mistake in the sed command. The pattern \'s/\\\'$ADMIN_USER\\\'/\\"$ADMIN_USER\\"/g\' is looking for the exact string \'$ADMIN_USER\' surrounded by single quotes. However, in the script, the variables are inside single quotes, so the actual string is \'$ADMIN_USER\', which is what the sed command is targeting. But maybe the sed command isn\'t matching because of the way the quotes are escaped. \n\nAlternatively, maybe the user should use a different approach, like using double quotes for the entire line or ensuring that all instances of single-quoted variables are replaced. Another thing to check is if the ConfigMap was successfully updated. After applying the changes, the user should verify the ConfigMap\'s data to ensure the variables are now in double quotes.\n\nIf the ConfigMap isn\'t updated correctly, the pods will still fail because the variables won\'t be expanded. The next step is to reapply the ConfigMap and then check the pod logs again to see if the script is now executing with the correct variables. If the issue persists, maybe there\'s another problem, like incorrect credentials or MongoDB not being ready when the script runs. But the main issue seems to be the variable interpolation, so fixing that should resolve the CrashLoopBackOff.\n</think>\n\n', additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl get pods -n hotel-reservation"}', 'name': 'exec_kubectl_cmd_safely'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-b4491859b1508673', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 685, 'prompt_tokens': 19227, 'total_tokens': 19912, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfad3-6f4c-7643-861d-41ffb23b328c-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_kubectl_cmd_safely', 'args': {'command': 'kubectl get pods -n hotel-reservation'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-b4491859b1508673', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 19227, 'output_tokens': 685, 'total_tokens': 19912}), ToolMessage(content='NAME                                     READY   STATUS             RESTARTS        AGE\nconsul-5c696cc4dc-6s4xr                  1/1     Running            0               9m36s\nfrontend-6df8475df4-qcb4d                1/1     Running            0               9m36s\ngeo-57c7bd6d5c-s9b66                     1/1     Running            2 (8m43s ago)   9m35s\njaeger-5b9775bd94-hgczs                  1/1     Running            0               9m32s\nmemcached-profile-6849578b8-hgpdc        1/1     Running            0               9m29s\nmemcached-rate-948594dfd-qlwq9           1/1     Running            0               9m24s\nmemcached-reserve-68dbb57476-8644q       1/1     Running            0               9m13s\nmongodb-geo-5d9cf968b9-ztqrl             0/1     CrashLoopBackOff   5 (114s ago)    7m10s\nmongodb-profile-76fb8d4b68-nl5tj         0/1     CrashLoopBackOff   5 (119s ago)    7m8s\nmongodb-rate-b9589b8d-n67gv              0/1     CrashLoopBackOff   