rror during initialization, likely due to the init script failing. Since the script is mounted in `/docker-entrypoint-initdb.d`, I need to check the container\'s logs directly to identify the exact error (e.g., authentication failure, syntax error, or user creation issues).  \n\ntool_call: {"command": "kubectl logs -n hotel-reservation mongodb-geo-5d9cf968b9-ztqrl --container hotel-reserv-geo-mongo"}', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': Usage(completion_tokens=605, prompt_tokens=27180, total_tokens=27785, completion_tokens_details=None, prompt_tokens_details=None), 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfad4-e318-7a11-880b-e30fc3d0c556-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 27180, 'output_tokens': 605, 'total_tokens': 27785}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='67f8f6f0-9fc9-4af2-a894-7242b41c94b1')]]
