any output from the failed container. Also, checking the events for the pod to see if there are any error messages related to the init container or the script execution. \n\nIf the logs don\'t show anything, maybe the script is not being executed at all, or the container is exiting immediately. In that case, the user might need to inspect the container\'s filesystem or check the init script\'s permissions. \n\nBut given the tools available, the best next step is to retrieve the logs again, ensuring that the script\'s output is captured. If the logs still don\'t show errors, the user might need to consider other factors like network issues or MongoDB configuration problems. However, based on the current information, the most likely cause is the init script failing due to incorrect credentials or authentication issues.\n</think>\n\n', additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl logs -n hotel-reservation mongodb-geo-5d9cf968b9-ztqrl --tail=-1"}', 'name': 'exec_kubectl_cmd_safely'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-90a045559d4146b8', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 717, 'prompt_tokens': 12228, 'total_tokens': 12945, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfad1-e597-7e42-9673-b72f86b386fd-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_kubectl_cmd_safely', 'args': {'command': 'kubectl logs -n hotel-reservation mongodb-geo-5d9cf968b9-ztqrl --tail=-1'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-90a045559d4146b8', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 12228, 'output_tokens': 717, 'total_tokens': 12945}), ToolMessage(content='{"t":{"$date":"2026-03-17T08:02:58.048+00:00"},"s":"I",  "c":"CONTROL",  "id":23285,   "ctx":"main","msg":"Automatically disabling TLS 1.0, to force-en